CloudBurrow patch 2 to github.com/goccy/go-googlesql v0.3.0
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1189).

The bug: the bindings have no way to build an absl::TimeZone, so
AnalyzerOptions.SetDefaultTimeZone could not be called, and the analyzer
kept its built-in default zone, America/Los_Angeles, where BigQuery's is
UTC. The patch adds UTCTimeZone(), a TimeZone of UTC: an absl::TimeZone
is one pointer to its zone's implementation, and a null one is UTC
(abseil's cctz: a default-constructed time_zone is "in effect UTC", and
utc_time_zone() returns one), so it is a zeroed block of wasm memory,
allocated once. SetDefaultTimeZone copies it. googlesqlite patch 0019
sets it; its test default_time_zone_utc_test.go fails without it.

